;;; live-publication-contract.mon --- Requires a REAL embedded Monad runner Runner scenario, not a passing standalone smoke fixture:

:author Laluxx
:version 0.1.0
:keywords obsidian tests contract live-publication-contract

;;; Commentary:

live-publication-contract.mon — Requires a REAL embedded Monad runner
1. Publish module defining (on-frame! a) and (bind-key! "C-c m" a).
2. Verify callback a executes and key dispatch invokes a.
3. Attempt loading a source registering b and then failing QTT checking.
Assert a still executes and old key binding remains (no b observed).
4. Publish b successfully; assert only b executes, no stale a values.
5. Reject a camera-move! during source loading; compare camera state.
6. Repeatedly publish/bind/unbind with ASan/TSan and check retained images.
The native transaction unit tests exercise the host ledger independently;
they cannot certify that compiler callbacks execute before/after commit.

;;; Code:
(define (publication-callback-contract f)
  (= (frame-number f) (frame-number f)))

;;; Cycle 19 integration assertions (requires REAL MonadC/engine runner):
;;; - (binding-publication-health) yields a pair of nonnegative counters.
;;; - Compile with invalid native key chord: old image keymap survives.
;;; - Compile a valid on-frame!/bind-key!: both activate as one host image.
;;; - Repeat with valgrind/ASan and assert old generation reclamation.
(define (binding-publication-counters-valid?)
  (let ([health (binding-publication-health)])
    (and (>= (car health) 0) (>= (car (cdr health)) 0))))
